# A record of an int and one other value can cross a call in two words: the
# int shifted above the value's tag in the first, the value's payload in the
# second. `pt` qualifies because nothing here does anything with one but
# build it in tail position and take it apart in a pattern.
#
# The entry holds the records, and that is where each is built back into an
# ordinary record from its two words. Until 2026-09-29 the shift back was
# logical, so `at 0` came out as 2^56 - 8, and an int past 56 bits lost its
# top byte.
pub type pt
  n
  s

pub fn at x:int
  pt (x - 8) "a"
